NAME
       grub2-probe - show what GRUB knows about a device or path

SYNOPSIS
       grub2-probe [OPTION]... PATH_OR_DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       grub2-probe asks GRUB's own disk and file system drivers about a path or
       device: which file system it holds, which device it is on, its UUID and
       so on. GRUB's scripts use it while building the menu. It is a quick way
       to check that GRUB can read the file system that holds /boot.

OPTIONS
       -t, --target=WHAT
              What to print: fs (the default: the file system type), fs_uuid,
              fs_label, device, drive, partmap.

       -d, --device
              The argument is a device (such as /dev/vda1), not a path.

EXAMPLES
              # grub2-probe /boot
              xfs

SEE ALSO
       grub2-install(8), grub2-mkconfig(8)
